        "curated_prompt": "wait_random_exponential does not respect its minimum wait\n\nThe configured minimum should be respected by the randomized exponential wait strategy. It currently still samples values below that minimum.\n\n```python\nfrom tenacity import Retrying, RetryCallState, wait_random_exponential\n\nretrying = Retrying()\nstate = RetryCallState(retrying, None, (), {})\nstate.attempt_number = 1\nwaiter = wait_random_exponential(min=5, multiplier=1)\nprint([waiter(state) for _ in range(5)])\n```\n\nFor this first-attempt configuration, the exponential wait bound is already limited to 5 seconds by the minimum setting. Each generated wait should therefore be 5.0 seconds. The current random interval starts at 0 and ends at 5, so waits below the requested minimum are possible.\n\nThe minimum must also remain respected for later attempts.\n",
